{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>El who brought them out of Egypt.</b> You said, 'Behold, a people has come out of Egypt' — they did not come out on their own, but Elohim brought them out." "<b>Like the lofty flights of the re'em for Him.</b> Like the strength of his height and loftiness. And likewise 'וְכֶסֶף תּוֹעָפוֹת' (Job 22) — they are a term for might. And I say that it is a term from 'וְעוֹף יְעוֹפֵף' (Genesis 1) — that which flies in height and loftiness has great strength; תּוֹעֲפֹת רְאֵם — the soaring of height. Another interpretation: תּוֹעֲפֹת רְאֵם — the strength of re'emim. And our Sages said: these are the demons (see Gittin 68)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:27.718052264Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}